# nodes-base conventions

Apply when editing `packages/nodes-base`.

## Node shape

- Follow the structure of the nearest maintained node version. Do not introduce a new node architecture when an existing local pattern applies.
- Prefer existing helpers in the node folder (`GenericFunctions`, etc.) over duplicating request/error logic.
- Keep parameter `displayName` / `description` clear; use `displayOptions` for conditional fields.

## Errors and parsing

- Prefer `NodeOperationError` / `NodeApiError` for user-facing failures — not bare `throw new Error(...)`.
- Prefer `jsonParse` (or project helpers) over raw `JSON.parse(` when policy lists that as preferred.
- Do not introduce `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error` to silence type issues in contribution fixes.

## Safety

- Never use untrusted `getNodeParameter` values as computed object keys in assignments; use safe helpers from `n8n-workflow` when grouping by user input.
- Do not change credentials files or auth flows unless the ticket area explicitly includes them and policy allows it.

## Scope

- Touch only files needed for the ticket acceptance criteria.
- Leave unrelated nodes, credentials, and package wiring alone.
